
==English==
[[File:Silver Gull mouth.jpg|thumb|right|A Silver Gull squawking]]
===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/skwɔːk/}}
* {{audio|en-us-squawk.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɔːk}}
* homophone: ''[[squark]]'' in non-rhotic dialects

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[shrill]] [[noise]], especially made by a [[voice]] or [[bird]]; a [[yell]], [[scream]], or [[call]].
# {{context|aviation|lang=en}} A four-digit transponder code used by aircraft for identification or transmission of emergency signals.
# {{context|aviation|lang=en}} An issue or complaint related to aircraft maintenance.
# The [[American night heron]].

====Translations====
{{trans-top|shrill noise}}
* German: {{t|de|Krächzen|n}}, {{t|de|Kreischen|n}}
* Spanish: {{t+|es|graznido|m}}, {{t|es|chillido|m}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Turkish: {{t+|tr|ciyaklama}}, {{t+|tr|viyaklama}}, {{qualifier|aviation}} {{t|tr|şikâyet etme}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To make a squawking noise; to [[yell]], [[scream]], or call out [[shrilly]].
#* {{RQ:Orwell Animal Farm|6}}
#*: The hens woke up '''squawking''' with terror because they had all dreamed simultaneously of hearing a gun go off in the distance.
# To [[speak]] [[out]]; to [[protest]].
# To [[report]] an [[infraction]]; to [[rat]] on or [[tattle]]; to [[disclose]] a [[secret]].
# {{context|aviation|lang=en}} To set or transmit a four-digit transponder code. {{non-gloss definition|(Normally followed by the specific code in question.)}}

